<p id="p2">If you didn’t follow the livestream of today’s Apple Surprise and Shine event, you can replay it on <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-events/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple’s Events site</a> or <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=39BalPDuTo0" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube</a>.</p>
<p id="p3">The keynote video <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-events/" rel="noopener noreferrer">can be streamed here</a> and <a href="https://tv.apple.com/us/movie/apple-event-090925/umc.cmc.6jpmnsmwtnusl1yeny90o2ui6" rel="noopener noreferrer">on the Apple TV using the TV app</a>. A high-quality version will also be available through Apple Podcasts as a <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/apple-events/id1473854035" rel="noopener noreferrer">video</a> and <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/apple-events/id1473854035" rel="noopener noreferrer">audio</a> podcast. An American Sign Language version of the event keynote is <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-events/" rel="noopener noreferrer">available on the Apple Events page too</a>.</p>
